********************************************************************************************************************************
* (A) DATA                                                                                                                     *
********************************************************************************************************************************
electrodes.dat                :: File of electrode coordinates
dataSynthetic.dat                      :: File of resistance measurements (data.dat). If synthetic data: dataSynthetic.dat
1                             :: Number of datasets with different noise parameterisation
datasets.dat                  :: File containing dataset associations (only used if number of datasets > 1)
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (B) OUTPUT FILES                                                                                                             *
********************************************************************************************************************************
samples.out                   :: File containing Voronoi models (gets renamed to e.g. samples.out1 for chain 1)
ncells.out                    :: File containing number of cells (gets renamed to e.g. ncells.out1 for chain 1)
sigmas.out                    :: File containing data noise parameters (gets renamed to e.g. noise.out1 for chain 1)
misfit.out                    :: File containing misfits (gets renamed to e.g. misfit.out1 for chain 1)
aratios.out                   :: File containing acceptance ratios (gets renamed to e.g. aratios.out1 for chain 1)
temper.out                    :: File containing temperature jumps
1                             :: Save residuals? (1=yes,0=no)
residuals.out                 :: File containing residuals (gets renamed to e.g. residuals.out1 for chain 1)
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (C) NUMBER OF MODEL PARAMETERS                                                                                               *
********************************************************************************************************************************
5                             :: Number of model parameters to be inverted 
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (D) PRIOR PARAMETERS                                                                                                         *
********************************************************************************************************************************
3   100                       :: Minimum and maximum number of Voronoi cells
0.6   10                      :: Minimum and maximum log10(resistivity) / fracture length
2                             :: Power law exponent for the distribution of the length
1.5  12.5                     :: Minimum and maximum x
0   0                         :: Minimum and maximum y (not used in 2D)
6   16                        :: Minimum and maximum z
1                             :: Noise parameterisation type
0.001   0.1                   :: Noise type 1,2: minimum and maximum noise parameter "a"
0.002   0.2                   :: Noise type 1,2: minimum and maximum noise parameter "b"
0.01   10                     :: Noise type 3,6: minimum and maximum noise parameter "lambda"
0.05   0.2                    :: Noise type 0: minimum and maximum noise parameter "sigma"
0.5866                        :: Noise type 6: standard deviation associated to the homogeneous matrix (no fracture) "sigma_mat"
12.5459                       :: Targetted apparent electrical resisitivty of the homegeneous matrix
1                             :: Add a model parameter (0=no option, 1=fracture angle, 2=fracture aperture)
0   360                       :: Minimum and maximum angle (degree). Required even if no model parameter is added (no option)
0.001   0.1                   :: Minimum and maximum aperture (meter). Required even if no model parameter is added (no option)
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (F) PROPOSAL PARAMETERS                                                                                                      *
********************************************************************************************************************************
1                             :: log10(resistivity) perturbation (0.6)
0.5                           :: log10(resistivity) perturbation for delayed rejection (0.3)
5  5  5                       :: Perturbation of x,y,z position (percentage of x,y,z prior range)
2  2  2                       :: Perturbation of x,y,z position for delayed rejection (percentage of x,y,z prior range)
0.2                           :: log10(resistivity) perturbation for birth step
0.3                           :: Perturbation of noise parameter "a"
0.2                           :: Perturbation of noise parameter "b"
0.2                           :: Perturbation of noise parameter "lambda"
0.5                           :: Perturbation of noise parameter "sigma"
5                             :: Perturbation of the optional parameter (percentage). Required even if no model parameter is added (no option)
2                             :: Perturbation of the optional parameter (percentage) for delayed rejections. Required even if no model parameter is added (no option)
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (G) LIKELIHOOD PARAMETERS                                                                                                    *
********************************************************************************************************************************
0                             :: Use Gaussian or Laplacian likelihood function? (0=Gaussian,1=Laplacian)
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (H) FORWARD MODELLING PARAMETERS
********************************************************************************************************************************
2                             :: Modelling method (1=fwd2_5D, 2=ERT_DDP_2.5D)
forward.in                    :: File containing forward modelling parameters for modelling method 1
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (I) MARKOV CHAIN PARAMETERS                                                                                                  *
********************************************************************************************************************************
0.3                           :: Maximum run time in hours
3                             :: Number of samples in this run
5000                          :: Total number of samples per chain including all runs (=0 to switch off this limit)
1                             :: Sample interval for displaying information in output file
1                             :: Add 1s sleep time between the display of each chain's information? (1=yes, 0=no)
0                             :: Run inversion without data? (1=yes,0=no)
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (J) PARALLEL TEMPERING PARAMETERS                                                                                            *
********************************************************************************************************************************
1                             :: Use parallel tempering? (1=yes,0=no)
0                             :: Jump type (0=random,1=near,2=nearest)
0                             :: Apply parallel tempering starting from this sample number
1   1                         :: Number of temperatures =1 and >1 (sum must be equal to total number of parallel chains)
8                             :: Temperatures >1 (one below the other) / 1st row = hottest temperature if nb temperatures>1 is > 2
7
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (K) PATH TO ert_ddp_2_5d REPOSITORY                                                                                          *
********************************************************************************************************************************
/home/leal/Desktop/Doctorat/Scripts/TransMontpInv/TransMontpInv/tdtomo_fortmtpi/source/forward/ert_ddp_2_5d/
********************************************************************************************************************************
* (L) TEMPORARY                                                                                         *
********************************************************************************************************************************
stdR3_config.dat                :: File of distances between electrodes M and N